  "chapter": 346,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 50 Chapter 346\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8834, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the family court act, in relation to the placement\n        of a former foster care youth during a certain state of emergen-\n        cy\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would create a new way for former foster youth  to  re-enter\nfoster  care  during the COVID-19 emergency without that added hurdle of\npetitioning the family court. This bill will allow vulnerable  youth  to\nreceive  the  supports and services that they need by creating a pathway\nto re-enter foster care without adding  to  the  currently  overburdened\nfamily court docket.\n \n  While  I  support  the  goals of this bill, there are technical issues\nthat could jeopardize federal funding if not corrected. The  Legislature\nhas  agreed to pass legislation in the upcoming session to correct these\ntechnical issues. On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased  to  sign\nthis bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2020
